{
  "_readme": [
    "Recitation of the morning & evening adhkar, mapped onto the dua ids in",
    "duas.json. Audio lives in assets/audio/adhkar/ as AAC-LC, 48 kbps, mono,",
    "44.1 kHz .m4a — AAC rather than Opus because Ogg/Opus will not play on",
    "iOS. Encode with:",
    "  ffmpeg -i in.wav -c:a aac -b:a 48k -ac 1 -ar 44100 out.m4a",
    "",
    "Several ids point at one file on purpose: 11 of the 36 morning/evening",
    "entries are the same Arabic word for word (the two sets share Ayat",
    "al-Kursi's neighbours, sayyidul-istighfar, the salawat, and so on), so 36",
    "entries need only 25 recordings — roughly six minutes in total.",
    "Deliberately NOT the near-identical pairs: ushhiduka and fitrah differ by",
    "asbahtu/amsaytu and get a recording each.",
    "",
    "A dua with no entry here simply has no audio: the session skips it and the",
    "listen affordance hides itself when a set has no coverage at all. That is",
    "what lets the feature ship dark until the recordings land."
  ],
